"content\\\": \\\"down<br>up\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">down the hill</span><br><span class=\\\"italic\\\">up the hill</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"bay\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"by\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">by the bay</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"river\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"by<br>near\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">by the river<span><br><span class=\\\"italic\\\">near the river</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"park\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"in<br>at<br>near\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">in the park</span><br><span class=\\\"italic\\\">at the park</span><br><span class=\\\"italic\\\">near the park</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"neighborhood\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"in\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">in Haight-Ashbury</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Saying How Far Places Are", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to know how far a place is, you can use the question: <span class=\"italic\">How far is \u2026 ?</span><br> You can reply with a specific distance if you know the answer, like <span class=\"italic\">It's 50 yards away</span>.<br> In North America, you use the imperial system, not the metric system.<br><br>If a place is nearby, you use yards to say how far it is.<br> If a place is far, you use miles to say how far it is.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"stron